    "type": "question",
    "label": "66",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\left(\\frac{2a^5}{3b^2}\\right)^{-3}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{27b^6}{8a^{15}}$, $a,b\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{2a^5}{3b^2}\\right)^{-3}&=\\left(\\frac{3b^2}{2a^5}\\right)^3\\\\\\left(\\frac{2a^5}{3b^2}\\right)^{-3}&=\\frac{27b^6}{8a^{15}}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator and negative power require $a,b\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
